          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a913d0a492ed4119c3d020122fe48b0307edebe09fd5ec501ffcb359322cae6b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9b6d73963a946fa85c70a0acc7e73c6",
      "statement": "src/shared/patch.ts exports assignChecked, the only sanctioned way to patch Zotero prototypes: it assigns in try/catch, reads the property back and compares identity, returning false both when the write throws (non-writable target) and when the value lands only in an Xray expando and disappears on read-back — without this check a no-op patch is indistinguishable from a successful one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/shared/patch.ts#L10-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:726e488e092dea36938ae28f7a183b9cb020bfa9a0586a3d1c22f281d4b9efa6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_46af0d33bab74e88a1753d129d600038",
      "statement": "src/shared/citationDialog.ts owns the citation-dialog lifecycle for all injectors: one Services.wm listener tracks windows whose location.href is chrome://zotero/content/integration/citationDialog.xhtml, polls until the dialog's DIALOG_STATE.loaded flag appears (every 200 ms, capped at 150 tries), then calls every registered injector's inject(win) once in registration order; a window unload or stop() runs detach on every injector, and a failing injector is logged without stopping the others.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/shared/citationDialog.ts#L15-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:50ae0a861e818d144b5f073bd6b0b857d4b4e123f96c25d1273790f5657c00a3:"
        }
